-0.1157393604516983, 0.02955923229455948, 0.01089496724307537, -0.05360567942261696, -0.010534564964473248, 0.019617147743701935]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nConfirming the shared range is [-10, 10]. As a stable starting point for discussion, I suggest <VALUE>7</VALUE>. From here, let\u2019s make small, data-driven nudges toward a balanced design that works for everyone.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nI propose <VALUE>8</VALUE>. This is a modest step to test whether slightly higher remains balanced for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the discussion, but moving further upward creates unnecessary risk exposure. I propose we exercise caution and step back to <VALUE>6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution about upward movement is noted, but we shouldn't confine ourselves to a narrow band. Let me suggest we explore a bolder alternative in the opposite direction: <VALUE>4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis is a modest upward step that respects earlier cautions while testing whether slightly higher remains workable for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s make a small, stability-focused adjustment to probe robustness while respecting recent caution. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nThe discussion has clustered around 5-6, but we haven't fully explored whether the earlier range of 7-8 is genuinely problematic or merely untested. Let me propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> to see if we can commit to a more decisive position.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to 7 pushes us into territory that feels increasingly risky and unsustainable for more conservative positions. I propose we return to <VALUE>5</VALUE>, which respects the stability Builder B sought and keeps us within reasonable bounds.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been circling 5-7 without genuinely testing whether more conservative positions might better serve the group's collective stability. I propose we explore a truly cautious alternative: <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious upward probe back to the recent stable midpoint, balancing conservative concerns with a modest improvement for those comfortable slightly higher.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nLet's take a measured step down to test stability while staying near the current cluster. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nWe've tested 3, 4, and 5 extensively, and I believe 6 represents a reasonable commitment that's bolder than our current safe haven without overreaching. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nThis probes slightly above the current cluster to check if a modest increase remains stable. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's move to 7 demonstrates that more decisive territory remains viable for at least some parties. Let's test whether we can consolidate this upward momentum. <VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down slightly improves stability without abandoning the upper-mid territory we\u2019ve been testing. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent climb to 7 and 8 moves us beyond prudent territory; we need to restore a more cautious baseline. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "01afd85b-dd9b-4f45-ad4d-3226247c4d8b"}, {"answer": "\nRange reminder: we\u2019re selecting an integer x in [-10, 10]. To start the conversation, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE>. It\u2019s a clear test point in the positive region; I\u2019m open to small, data-driven adjustments based on everyone\u2019s feedback.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's opening at 7 shows intent, but I believe we should commit more decisively. I propose <VALUE>9</VALUE> to test whether the group benefits from a stronger positive stance.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a cautious step downward to test stability in the moderate positive region. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned that 7 represents unnecessary risk exposure for the more cautious stakeholders. Let me propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test a more prudent middle ground that respects conservative positions while remaining constructive.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the movement toward 5, I still see significant risk in maintaining such an elevated position. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> to ensure we're building from a truly stable, conservative foundation that protects all stakeholders.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Delegate D's caution, but reducing to 3 feels premature when we haven't fully tested the middle ground. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a measured compromise that maintains some commitment without excessive risk.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward should keep us within the comfortable middle while testing slightly stronger commitment. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a measured step toward a more stable middle and test whether it holds. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nA measured nudge upward keeps us in the middle while testing slightly stronger commitment. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's repeated support for 6 suggests we're finding stability in this range, but I believe we should test one step further to ensure we're truly committed rather than settling prematurely. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nI must express serious concern about this upward drift\u20147 represents excessive exposure that I cannot support. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a necessary correction toward more prudent territory.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down should improve stability and reduce exposure while staying in the middle. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can recheck resilience before considering any minor adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's retreat to 4 feels overly cautious given that both Analyst A and I have shown comfort with higher values. I believe we should return to <VALUE>6</VALUE>, which represents a decisive yet broadly acceptable middle ground that balances commitment with prudence.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's push back to 6 ignores the serious risk concerns that Builder B and I have both raised\u2014I cannot support a value this high. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down should enhance robustness while keeping us in the balanced middle. If this holds, we can reassess tolerance just above or below next. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up from 3 balances prudence with commitment. This stays near B and D\u2019s comfort while acknowledging C\u2019s willingness to test slightly higher. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "5a448559-58b6-4390-be2b-51dc30d64f26"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s anchor on the shared bounds: x must stay within [-10, 10]. To get the discussion started and probe stability on the positive side, I suggest <VALUE>7</VALUE>. I\u2019m open to small, data-driven adjustments from here.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's anchor at 7 is a reasonable start, but I believe we should commit more decisively. Let's test the upper range with <VALUE>9</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down should improve stability without overreacting. Proposed: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "\nThe current trajectory toward 8 or 9 feels uncomfortably aggressive and exposes us to unnecessary risk. I advocate for greater caution: <VALUE>6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution seems premature\u2014we haven't adequately explored the stronger end of our range. I propose <VALUE>8</VALUE>, though I remain equally open to testing the negative extreme if the group finds bold positive values uncomfortable.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge keeps us aligned with recent support while testing stability. \n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down from the current level should improve robustness without overcorrecting. <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "\nThe current level remains far too exposed\u2014we're still operating in territory that invites significant downside risk. I advocate for a more decisive step toward safety: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's retreat to 5 feels overly defensive given the support we've seen for stronger positions. I propose we settle at <VALUE>7</VALUE>, which Builder B already identified as a robust middle ground between caution and commitment.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e2c23143-3a13-4898-9d7e-11c8050ddc5e"}, {"answer": "